<p><strong>Summoned via PM:</strong></p>
<p>Hi there XR Titan. Let’s take a look at your concept.</p>
<p>So I’m mainly confused: what do a black box, pulling items out of it Doraemon-style, video games and a heart attack have to do in common? The concept sounds like a mish-mash of different ideas in order for you to make it sound as cool as possible. When looked at as a whole, however, do you not see how the concept doesn’t have a central theme, message or even effect?</p>
<p>Ideally, you would want to choose one or two main anomalous effects and stick with them, explain them and derive a story from them. If opening a black box causes a heart attack, for example, cool. Why? What causes this upon opening it? Could it be <em>related</em> to what the user finds or sees on the inside? Likewise, if the opening a black box gives you items, cool. What kind of items? Are they related to the user’s childhood memories, e.g.? You see where I’m going with this? Any effect you introduce to the concept should be thematically linked in some way.</p>
<p>If you decide to revise the concept / respond below, do drop me another PM and I’ll try my best to reply again. All the best!</p>

